document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
  const neonTexts = document.querySelectorAll(".neon-text");

  neonTexts.forEach((element) => {
    const neonColor = element.getAttribute("data-neon-color");

    // Function to calculate complementary background color
    function getComplementaryColor(hex) {
      const r = parseInt(hex.slice(1, 3), 16);
      const g = parseInt(hex.slice(3, 5), 16);
      const b = parseInt(hex.slice(5, 7), 16);

      // Invert RGB values for a complementary background
      const invR = 255 - r;
      const invG = 255 - g;
      const invB = 255 - b;

      return `rgb(${invR}, ${invG}, ${invB})`;
    }

    // Set CSS variables for dynamic use in CSS
    element.style.setProperty("--neon-color", neonColor);
    element.style.setProperty("--bg-color", getComplementaryColor(neonColor));

    // Toggle active class on click
    element.addEventListener("click", () => {
      element.classList.toggle("active");
    });
  });
});
```

---

## ✅ How It Works:

- Each `.neon-text` element has a `data-neon-color` attribute.
- On click, the `.active` class is toggled.
- The `--neon-color` and `--bg-color` **CSS variables** are set dynamically.
- The `.active` class applies:
  - Neon color to the text.
  - Complementary background color.
  - A **neon glow** using `box-shadow` with increasing intensity.

---

## ✅ Example Output

When you click on a text box:

- It smoothly transitions to the neon color.
- The background becomes a complementary color.
- A glowing effect surrounds the text, increasing in intensity.

---

## ✅ Customization Tips

- You can adjust the glow intensity in CSS by modifying the `box-shadow` values.
- You can add animations (e.g., blinking) for extra neon effect.
- You can use `@keyframes` to animate the glow if you want pulsing neon.

